  "Question": "For the quadratic function $y=-x^2-4x+1$, over what range of $x$ does $y$ increase as $x$ increases?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "$x>-2$",
    "B": "$x<-2$",
    "C": "$x>2$",
    "D": "$x<2$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Completing the square gives $y=-(x+2)^2+5$. The parabola opens downward, and its axis of symmetry is $x=-2$. For a downward-opening parabola, $y$ increases as $x$ increases to the left of the axis of symmetry, so $x<-2$.",
